'''Narkina 2'''<ref name="Season2">{{InsiderCite|233|Andor Season 2 Companion|''Andor'' Season 2 Companion}}</ref> was a location in<ref name="Planetnamia2" /> the [[Narkina system]] of the [[Abrion sector]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="Appendix" /> It was the site of an [[Unidentified Imperial factory facility (Dedra Meero)|Imperial factory facility]] where former [[ISB Supervisor|supervisor]] of the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] [[Dedra Meero]] was [[Prisoner|incarcerated]] by the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="Season2" /> after she was found to have acquired confidential files relating to [[Project Stardust]] that she did not have clearance for<ref name="Who Else">{{Andor|Who Else Knows?}}</ref> in [[1 BBY]].<ref name="Date">{{AndorDate|212}}</ref> Following a shift during her incarceration in that [[prison]], Meero sat in her cellblock and remained composed until the lights in her cellblock turned off&mdash;upon which she broke down crying.<ref name="Jedha Kyber Erso" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|It's probably Narkina 7 or Narkina 2. It's the women's version.|Tony Gilroy, on Dedra Meero's prison|<ref name="EW">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/andor-creator-tony-gilroy-explains-surprise-ending-final-shot-11731474|text=''Andor'' creator Tony Gilroy explains that surprise ending and final shot|author=Dalton Ross|date=2025-05-14|archivedate=20250516141415}}</ref>}}
[[File:SW-Insider-233-Final.jpg|thumb|right|200px|''Star Wars Insider'' 233, which first identified Narkina 2]]
Narkina 2 first appeared, albeit unidentified, in "[[Jedha, Kyber, Erso]],"<ref name="Jedha Kyber Erso" /> the series finale of the [[Disney+]] live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', which was released on [[May 13]], [[2025]]. It was later identified in the ''[[Star Wars Insider]]'' magazine article [[Andor Season 2 Companion|''Andor'' Season 2 Companion]] by [[Lucas O. Seastrom]] and [[Jay Stobie (real person)|Jay Stobie]]. The article was published in [[Star Wars Insider 233|''Star Wars Insider'' 233]]<ref name="Season2" /> on [[August 19]] of the same year.<ref name="Titan">{{TitanComics|url=m/183-star-wars-insider-233|text=Star Wars Insider #233}}</ref>

Previously, the name "Narkina 2" had appeared as a typo of [[Narkina 5]] in a [[StarWars.com]] article written by [[Kristin Baver]] and published on [[May 14]], 2025, in which the prison where Dedra Meero was stated to be "reminiscent of Narkina 2,"<ref name="Explained">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-finale-episodes-10-11-12|text=''Andor'' Explained: Episodes 10-12 - "Make It Stop", "Who Else Knows?", and "Jedha, Kyber, Erso"}}</ref> in apparent reference to the [[Unidentified Imperial factory facility|Imperial prison]] located on Narkina 5 shown in [[Andor Season 1|''Andor'' Season 1]].<ref name="Narkina 5">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}}</ref> When discussing Meero's prison in an [[Wikipedia:Entertainment Weekly|''Entertainment Weekly'']] interview published the same day as the StarWars.com article, the series' creator [[Tony Gilroy]] described Meero's prison as hypothetically being Narkina 2 or Narkina 7 as a [[Gender|all-female]] prison as opposed to Narkina 5.<ref name="EW" /> Gilroy had also previously mentioned Narkina 2 as a hypothetical location for the Empire's [[alien]] prisoners when discussing Narkina 5 in an interview with [[Wikipedia:Valnet#Collider|''Collider'']] on [[November 22]], [[2022]].<ref name="Collider">{{WebCite|url=https://collider.com/andor-aliens-explained-tony-gilroy-comments|text=Why 'Andor' Doesn't Have Many 'Star Wars' Aliens Explained By Showrunner Tony Gilroy [Exclusive&#93;|author=Maggie Lovitt|date=2022-11-22|work=[[Wikipedia:Valnet#Collider|''Collider'']]|archivedate=20250315010102}}</ref>

